[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Bishop's Opening"]
[Variation "Bishop's Opening: 3.Qf3"]
[ECO "C23"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "fork,early-queen"]
[Themes "tempo-on-queen,develop-first"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3.Qf3"]
[Start "bishops-opening 3.Qf3 Nf6"]

4. d3 { Guards e4, but the queen on f3 and the pawn on c2 are both loose. } ( 4. c3 Be7 { With c3 covering d4, Black simply develops and castles. } 5. d3 Na5 { Asks the bishop to move, so Black can trade it off for the knight later. } ) ( 4. Ne2 Na5 { Goes after the bishop on c4, White's best attacker. } ) ( 4. Nc3 Nd4 { Attacks the queen and the pawn on c2 at once. } 5. Qd1 c6 { Prepares ...d5, which takes the centre and hits the bishop. } ) ( 4. Nh3 Nd4 5. Qd1 d5 { Opens the centre while White's pieces are on bad squares. } ) ( 4. g4 Nd4 5. Qd1 d5 ) ( 4. Qb3 Nd4 { Hits the queen again. If Bxf7+, the king takes on e7 and White cannot keep both the queen and the bishop safe. } 5. Bxf7+ Ke7 ) 4... Nd4 { Attacks the queen and the pawn on c2 at once, so White has to spend another move on the queen. } 5. Qd1 d5 { Takes the centre and hits the bishop. White has made three queen and pawn moves and has nothing developed. } *
